finding: The public hook is not yet true under exceptions or restore reentrancy. (1) world.ts add notifies from finally even when defaults/value writes/required adds failed. Reproducer: Bad=component('bad',{v:f32},{defaults:()=>{throw Error('boom')}}); C=component('c',{v:f32}); A=component('a',{v:f32},{requires:[Bad,C]}); register all, observe A, add(create(),A). The A observer receives true with Bad.v=0 and C absent. Likewise a supplied value getter throwing midway produces an attachment notification with only partially written values. This contradicts 'after defaults and values ... and missing required companions are added'. Decide and document exception semantics and test them rather than announcing completion from finally. (2) The new refusal itself can leave World inconsistent when propagated. Add C with v=42; cache query([C]); observe C with (_,present)=>{if(!present)world.add(eid,C)}; try world.remove(eid,C), or world.destroy(eid), and catch outside. The promised refusal throws, but has(C)=false while query still yields eid and C.v remains 42; destroy also leaves eid alive. Their cleanup is after, not in, the notification try/finally. Existing refusal tests catch inside the observer and hide this path. (3) restore is not guarded during notification. Register C and stateless recovery, allocate its storage, create eid, snapshot while C absent; observe C with (eid,p)=>{if(p)world.restore(snapshot)} and install a second observer recording [p,world.has(eid,C)]; world.add(eid,C). The second observer sees [false,false], then [true,false]. A truthful notification contract needs to refuse or safely handle restore during an active notification and guard membership mutations during restore notifications. Reproducers were independently run on 4636a7c4; /tmp/membership-probe.ts and /tmp/membership-failures.ts contain them. No tracked files edited. ECS 124/124, observer set 14/14, physics bridge/common set 436/436 pass; the new attachment/other-changes/refusal tests fail at 33b88804 while restore test already passes. These checks do not exercise the failing paths above.
